Revision history for WWW-MikroTik

{{$NEXT}}
    - Initial release
    - WWW::MikroTik: a single Moo class for the MikroTik RouterOS REST API
      (https://<router>/rest), HTTP Basic auth over LWP::UserAgent
    - RouterOS verbs list, add, set, remove, cmd and print, on top of the
      plain HTTP verbs get, put, patch, delete and post and the request core
    - print takes proplist and query for the POST form of the console print
      (.proplist / .query)
    - Values pass through as the strings RouterOS sends and expects; nothing
      is converted in either direction
    - A response status of 400 or higher croaks with the status, message and
      detail of the router's JSON error object, or with the HTTP status line
      when there is none (non-JSON body, unreachable router, TLS error)
    - A success status with a body that is not JSON croaks with the module
      prefix, the status line and the decoder's reason
    - ua attribute as the seam for a custom or mock user agent; request
      logging through Log::Any
    - Secret-looking fields are masked in the debug log: any top-level body
      key or query parameter whose name contains password, passphrase,
      secret, token or psk, or is key or ends in -key (private-key,
      pre-shared-key, auth-key, ...), except public-key; the request itself
      is sent unchanged
    - set and remove send the id as a single path segment: %, # and ? are
      escaped, so set('/interface', 'vlan#1', ...) addresses vlan#1 and not
      vlan; the * of an .id stays literal
    - The request path and query keys and values are character strings,
      encoded as UTF-8 like the JSON body: the same text gives the same URL
      whatever Perl's internal string representation
